{\*\ftnsep\chftnsep}\pgndec\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\loch
Pipeline is designed to simple, lightweight, and work on SLURM}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\loch
The sacrifice is that it is not necessarily flexible or scalable to be operated by many people. }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\loch
It is designed to work for thousands of lightning flashes. Not necessarily tens of thousands. }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\loch
It's primary purpose is to have a linear set of steps to be performed automatically on a large number of flashes, operated by one-person. The stage at which a flash is injected and precisaly what happens at end (if it is completely removed after processing, or raw data is kept) is slightly flexable so that other people on the system can use the data if they desire. }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\loch
The pipeline has two major components, the database and the processor. }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\loch
Much of the behavior of the database and processor are controlled by the settings file. This is discussed later. }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\rtlch\afs48 \ltrch\loch\fs48\loch
1) The Database}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\loch
"the database" is two JSON files that each hold a panda's dataframe. Stored using "SDF.to_json(orient='table')" python function. }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\loch
This is chosen so that it is simple and easy to read. The information in the database is designed to guide the processor, and inform what imaging stage the flash is in. It is NOT designed to store information about scientific quality. (e.g. location, image quality, flash type, science notes, etc...)}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\loch
The location database is stored in the settings file.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\rtlch\afs36 \ltrch\loch\fs36\loch
1.A) stormDatabase}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\loch
One table, "stormDatabase" holds information about "storms", which is a single contiguous observation period of LOFAR. The rows are:}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
'LTAloc_file', 'MD5Sum_file', 'year', 'month', 'day', 'hour, "ID_prefix"(eg:  L2025065), "numberFlashes"}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
The majority of which are strings. year, month, day, hour, are each two digit strings (so that the leading zero is maintained); and they correspond to the observation time of the first flash in the observation (NOT the start of observation, which isn't really known). }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
The key is the storm name, which consists of the last two digits of a year and letters. E.G. "19A".  The letters should be assigned so they are in order of storm observation, but this is not a requirment. (Sometimes we get information for storm after later storms).}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
'LTAloc_file' and 'MD5Sum_file' are file names that are relative. The folder is controlled by the settings file (see below). Both are optional. }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\rtlch\afs36 \ltrch\loch\fs36
  }{\rtlch\afs36 \ltrch\loch\fs36\loch
1.B) flash Database}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
The other table is "flashDatabase". It is far more important, and holds information about each individual flash. The rows are:}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
   }{\loch
'TimeID', 'year', 'month', 'day', 'state', 'sub_state', 'rawDataDownloaded', 'calibration_file', 'pipeline_priority', 'pipeline_mode', 'deleteData_on_complete', 'slurm_processes', 'storm'}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
   }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
Where:  'TimeID', 'year', 'month', 'day', 'state', 'sub_state', calibration_file', 'pipeline_mode', and 'storm'}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
\tab are strings.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
And: 'rawDataDownloaded', 'deleteData_on_complete'  are booleans}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
and: 'pipeline_priority' is an integer}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\loch
The key is a string of form flashname "-" integer. E.G. "19A-1". The integer should be in order of flash observation inside the storm, but this isn't required.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\loch
'TimeID' is of form D20190424T194432.504Z OR D20190424T194432  The decimal component is prefered but not required. 'year', 'month' and 'day' are all 2-digit strings. }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
'rawDataDownloaded' is TRUE if data has been downloaded and is available to use. }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
'calibration_file' is the name and locaiton of the calibration.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
\tab NOT YET DESIGNED: if calibration file is absolute or relative location. It is also not designed how to inject LOFAR2.0 calibration files. }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
If 'pipeline_priority' is higher, than this flash should be processed before flashes of lower number. The typical number is 5. negative numbers are allowed. Note The processor has no subtly in handling this. If a priority 6 flash is injected, it will get all processing power in needs, and all priority 5 flashes will wait if necessary. Even if there is a priority 5 flash that is one step from being done. It should be noted that within same priority level, flashes with later processing stage will be given priority.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
'deleteData_on_complete' is a boolean, default TRUE. If TRUE data will be deleted once pipeline is run}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
\tab NOT YET DESIGNED: if only raw data is deleted, or processed data too.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
\tab }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }{\loch
'storm' is a string of the storm name. Is the first part of the flash name}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{
 }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081{\loch
The rest of the data are for controlling the pipeline.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\loch

