There are some codes designed to work with the database outside of the processor. Each of these codes accesses the database via LoLIM.database.database_manager class. This class essentially makes a an empty file when it opens the database. It also checks if such an empty file exist, and if so does not open the database. In this way the database is (mostly) prevented to be opened by different programs. This technique has a weakness that it checks if file exists, and then makes a new empty-check file if none exists. In between those two moments it is possible for a different program to make the same checks. Thus, if two programs try to open the database at the same it is possible they could both succeed. So don\uc2 \u8217\'81\'66t do that. It is unclear how to fix this.\uc1 }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af5\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f5\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af7\langfe1081\loch

